{"name":"Saladin","hex":"#7e8f69","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Saladin","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The first sultan of Egypt and Syria and the founder of the Ayyubid dynasty, who led the Muslim opposition to the European crusaders in the Levant.","A governorate in northern Iraq."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Saladin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Saladin","blocks":[{"text":"Salah ad-Din Yusuf ibn Ayyub, commonly known as Saladin, was the founder of the Ayyubid dynasty and the first sultan of both Egypt and Syria. A Sunni Muslim ruler of Kurdish origin, Saladin was an important figure of the Third Crusade and spearheaded the Muslim military effort against the Crusader states in the Levant. At the height of his power, the Ayyubid realm spanned Egypt, Syria, Upper Mesopotamia, the Hejaz, Yemen, and Nubia."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Al-Nasir_I_Salah_al-Din_Yusuf_%28Saladin%29._AH_564-589_%281169-1193_CE%29_%C3%86_Dirham_%2830.1mm%2C_13.28_g%2C_6h%29._Without_mint-name._Dated_AH_586_%28AD_1190-91%29._Sultan_sitting_facing%2C_cross-legged%2C_on_high-backed_throne_%28obverse%29.jpg/330px-thumbnail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saladin"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Palmer_cup_left_attendants_%28British_Museum%29.jpg/500px-Palmer_cup_left_attendants_%28British_Museum%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Palmer_cup_left_attendants_%28British_Museum%29.jpg/500px-Palmer_cup_left_attendants_%28British_Museum%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ayyubid or Zengid soldiers in Seljuk-type clothes[24] and sharbush hats[25][26] on the Palmer Cup (1200–1215)[27]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/